# netsurf: a selector the sibling parser cannot read, with no sibling syntax in it, no longer makes the whole sheet conservative (patch 412)
# Generated 2026-11-08
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 411)
#
# The census's "sibling combinator may restyle on insert/remove" (9:
# cnnlite 4, rte 2, google, oldreddit, wpblog). A debug build (scratch
# only): every one came through html_rl_block_sibling_risk's state-2 exit
# -- a "conservative" sheet declines every block insert or removal that is
# not at the parent's tail. A sheet becomes state 2 when ONE selector
# prelude fails to parse (an escaped class name, .md\:flex, among others)
# anywhere in it.
#
#  - html_rl_prelude_sib_free: the failed prelude's text holds no sibling
#    combinator (a + or ~ outside [...] and strings, escapes skipped; a +
#    inside parentheses still counts), no :empty and no :has(.
#  - html_rl_scan_sheet: such a prelude yields no rule and the sheet stays
#    precise (its partial results freed). Every reader of the cache --
#    186's class check, 198's insert/remove check, 370/409's style check,
#    373's :empty check -- reads only those constructs.
#
# cnnlite (scratch build): 4 declines -> 0, its 4 block changes placed
# locally. rte, google, oldreddit keep theirs (their unreadable preludes
# hold sibling syntax, or the risk is real).
#
